* Circuit-breaker interruption: a gas-blast breaker clears a fault by chopping it, and the
* chopped current rings into the recovery voltage.
*
* Two identical circuits, each a 10 kV, 50 Hz source behind 31.8 mH of line inductance (a 1 kA
* symmetrical fault; switched in at the voltage zero, so the current is fully offset and first
* passes zero at ~20 ms), 10 nF across the breaker. The contacts part at 3 ms and travel 20 mm by
* 7 ms, compressing a 0.2 l puffer of SF6 at 5 bar (`ap=2e-3`) that the arc also heats.
*   X1  blast on (`k_blast=1e7`): the cooling grows with the gas the puffer blows across the arc;
*   X2  blast off: natural cooling only (20 kW at full travel).
*
* Mayr's arc voltage rises as P / I while the current falls toward zero, and a strongly cooled
* arc drives its own current to zero before the natural zero: current chopping. The current
* the inductor still carries then rings into the 10 nF, around the source voltage, with an
* amplitude energy conservation fixes: A = sqrt((v_c - V_src)^2 + (L/C) I_chop^2).
* What to look for (measured at 2.16.2+1; docs/examples/multiphysics/breaker_plots.py):
*   X1 chops 4.404 A at 19.144 ms; the recovery voltage peaks at -16,969 V (closed form -17,203 V);
*   X2 chops 3.652 A at 19.225 ms, peaking at -14,828 V (closed form -15,060 V).
*   The closed form is 1.5 % high in both: it holds the source voltage still over the 56 us
*   half-ring, and the arc's conductance does not vanish at the instant chosen.
*   The blast's trade-off: stronger cooling clears earlier and chops more current, so it
*   produces the higher overvoltage.
* Plot: python docs/examples/multiphysics/breaker_plots.py target/release/va-cli
* Run: va-cli sim circuits/multiphysics/breaker_interrupt.net --model models/multiphysics/breaker --tran --report p1,p2
VS1 s1 gnd SIN(0 10k 50)
L1 s1 p1 31.8m
C1 p1 gnd 10n
VS2 s2 gnd SIN(0 10k 50)
L2 s2 p2 31.8m
C2 p2 gnd 10n
VT trav gnd PWL(0 -1m 3m -1m 7m 20m)
X1 p1 gnd trav breaker k_blast=1e7 ap=2e-3
X2 p2 gnd trav breaker k_blast=0 ap=2e-3
.tran 20u 25m
.end
